# The many lights scene (see docs/rendering/global-illumination.md#world-probes): a low, dark hall of 64 point lights
# on an 8 x 8 grid, each of its own color, between a floor, a ceiling and two long walls, under no sun. The hits of the
# world probes and the split cascades pick one of the lights around them for each ray, so the light that each light
# sends to the ceiling bounces down onto the floor around it, from every light, not only the brightest few. Positions are raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m. The editor writes this file;
# see docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
